                  "id": "6d5afc09-9f93-4418-9c93-4dce6ebf8a09",
                  "title": "Customer Denies Initiating Transaction",
                  "status": "Open",
                  "severity": "Medium",
                  "type": "Repudiation",
                  "description": "A customer completes a purchase, receives the goods, then disputes the charge claiming they never placed the order. If the platform has no detailed audit trail — timestamps, IP addresses, session IDs tied to each transaction — there's no evidence to counter the claim.",
                  "mitigation": "Implement comprehensive transaction logging — log customer ID, session token, IP, timestamp, order details, and payment gateway reference ID for every transaction. Store logs in a tamper-evident, append-only store. This provides non-repudiation evidence for dispute resolution.",
